Marvel Nemesis recomp — Windows alpha and source code

This is an unofficial project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Marvel,
Electronic Arts, Microsoft, or the original developers. Game names and
trademarks belong to their respective owners. No original game executables,
usable game assets, generated game sources, prepared game-code DLLs or
community texture packs are included. The Windows package contains the host
EXE and compiler tools; game code is generated locally from the player's XBE.

The port is built on TGP482/XboxXBERecomp (MIT; sdk/LICENSE).
The bundled SDK has local modifications for this game and is not an
unmodified upstream release. Source provenance is recorded privately by
the maintainer; the development repository/history is not bundled here.

SMAA shader and generic lookup tables: iryoku/smaa, via the SCDA-XBERecomp
packaging at e8f8b443e97cc89c8b1f009df5b6b66e50a771ee.
GTAO integration includes code adapted from that SCDA revision.
Full notices are retained in the corresponding headers and docs/licenses/.

First-launch DLL preparation, import/export layout and freestanding headers
are adapted from TGP482/SCDA-XBERecomp V2, commit
70d8cac24460514cbb24a0252213d34ebc7b9a28 (MIT).
Bundled Clang/LLD use the LLVM license in docs/licenses/.

Build dependencies: Zydis and Zycore (MIT), toml++ (MIT), Dear ImGui (MIT),
and SDL (zlib). Full license texts are in docs/licenses/ and
sdk/THIRD_PARTY.txt. These dependencies are fetched by CMake; their source
trees are fetched for developer builds. The Windows package includes the
recompiler and statically linked dependencies, retaining these notices.

XboxXBERecomp also credits XenonRecomp, xemu and Cxbx-Reloaded as technical
references; see sdk/README.md. Original game data and trademarks are not
licensed by the software licenses supplied with this source repository.

